Model checkpoints
=================

Each model lives in its own folder, checkpoints/<name>_res/, holding fixed_weights.pth
(the two 145M models) or model_fixed_Van_checkpoint.pth (the four ablation models).
Evaluate one with:

    python eval_mymodels.py --model <name>                          # SRBench
    python eval_mymodels.py --model <name> --benchmark llmsrbench   # LLM-SRBench

Folder names read <params>_<max formula length>_simp<0|1>[_float][_ftnoise_...]:
simp1 = targets simplified to canonical form, float = constants not restricted to the
symbolic set, ftnoise = further trained on noise-corrupted targets.

Folder                                   Model
---------------------------------------  -------------------------------------------------
145M_80_simp1_float_ftnoise_48h_res      Our transformer ("ours" in every figure and table):
                                         145M parameters, formulae up to 80 tokens,
                                         simplified targets, further trained for 48 h on
                                         noise-corrupted targets (epsilon ~ U(0, 0.1), half
                                         the formulae noise-free, peak LR 5e-5).
145M_80_simp1_float_res                  The same transformer before fine-tuning on noisy
                                         targets; the fine-tuning above resumes from it.

Ablation: affine transformation x simplification (89M parameters, trained from scratch
on up to 120M data instances; "prefac" = affine transformation):

prefac_on_t120M_res                      affine = on,  simplification = on
prefac_on_nosimp_t120M_res               affine = on,  simplification = off
prefac_off_t120M_res                     affine = off, simplification = on
simp_off_t120M_res                       affine = off, simplification = off
